# Implement `src/extract.ts` — three-signal dependency extractor

## Context

We need to derive a tool-to-tool dependency graph from raw Composio JSON for the `googlesuper` (438 tools) and `github` (867 tools) toolkits. The extractor is the foundation of the whole project — graph quality, LLM augmentation, and visualization all consume its output. Output schemas in the raw data are name-only (`$ref` to undefined `$defs`), so we cannot reason from response payload structure. We must rely on three signals derived from inputs and prose.

**Ground-truth checks already done against `data/raw/*.json`:**
- All 44 hardcoded slugs in the spec exist in the dataset (0 missing).
- The trigger-pattern regex finds 151 mentions across descriptions; 14 direct slug matches; 36 `GMAIL_*` mentions that all normalize cleanly to existing `GOOGLESUPER_*` slugs.
- 11 tools carry a `file_uploadable: true` parameter — these are the consumers for the upload soft dep.

## Files modified

- [src/types.ts](src/types.ts) — add `DependencyEdge`, `DependencyConfidence`, `DependencyType`.
- [src/extract.ts](src/extract.ts) — replace stub with full implementation below.

No other files touched. `src/index.ts` is **not** modified by this task (the user will wire `extractDependencies` in a later step).

